# testsuite_examples for BASIC256
#
# Opens every program in Examples/Original_Examples, one at a time, in its own
# BASIC-256 window, so a person can check by eye that each one still works.
# After each example is closed it asks whether it worked, and at the end it
# lists every example that did not.
#
# testsuite_examples_ci.txt is the CI version: the examples that can run with
# nobody watching, each started with `basic256 -s` by
# .github/scripts/run_examples.sh and run_examples.ps1.
#
# Left out here as well as from CI:
#   networking/netserver.kbs and netclient.kbs only work as a pair running at
#       the same time, and SYSTEM waits for one program to finish before the
#       next can start - run netserver first, then netclient, by hand
#   testing/global_array_test.kbs, testing/test_slice.kbs and
#       testing/testimagesave.kbs no longer run on the current interpreter
#       (CALL without brackets, an old PUTSLICE form, IMGSAVE to GIF)
#
# Modification History
# date		programmer	description
# 20261004	m.vilain	original coding

include "testsuite_common_include.kbs"

currentsuite = "examples"

###################################################
call section("Original Examples")
###################################################

print "Each example opens in a BASIC-256 window of its own and starts running."
print "Read what to look for, try it, then close that window."
print "You are then asked whether it worked."
print
print "Before you start, check the preferences of THIS window:"
print "On the 'Advanced' tab"
print "  'Allow SYSTEM statement' must be allow, or you are asked about every example"
print
call different("Allow SYSTEM Statement", getSetting("SYSTEM","Allow/System"),0)

# Each entry is "path|what to look for", the path relative to
# Examples/Original_Examples.
dim examples(1)
examples = {
